{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfhdF6VFuuZVMrzdPjWcE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All three candidate files are written, and the self-check now prints `OK` with a finite ELPD-LOO of −1026.2. That's close to the current best model's −1023.0, but it comes from a 1-chain, 100-draw smoke fit, so treat the comparison as rough.\n\n**The hypothesis** (`adaptive_transition_learner_surprise`): people read each sequence flip by flip while an online learner predicts whether the next flip will repeat or switch. It starts from a prior guess (which may favour switching) and updates that guess from the transitions it has seen so far. A sequence looks random to the extent the learner stays surprised. Streaks become predictable as they go on, and so does perfect alternation once a few switches have been seen. This targets the critique's FDR-surviving discrepancy: perfect alternation is chosen as random more often than the current best model predicts. Each person has their own decisiveness, drawn from a population distribution.\n\n**The model:** a prior switch probability `theta` (Beta(4,4)), a prior strength `c` (in pseudo-transitions), and a non-centred log-normal population of per-person `beta` with 400 slots. It uses `compute_features` over at most 7 padded transitions per sequence.\n\n**Two fixes were needed to pass the check:**\n- **Saturated predictions:** `p_left` could reach exactly 0 or 1, so it is now clipped to (1e-6, 1−1e-6), and the prior on the average decisiveness is tighter.\n- **Near-ties:** when two sequences' surprisal differed only by floating-point noise, the leave-one-out estimate came out as NaN. Differences below 1e-9 are now set to exactly zero.\n\n**Risks for admission:**\n- **Speed:** the smoke fit took 167 s for just 200 iterations. The full admission fit is much longer, so it could run past the 30-minute limit per sampling run.\n- **Reliability:** 5.9% of trials had a high Pareto k, above the 1% tolerance, so its ELPD-LOO may be reported as unreliable.\n- **Convergence:** a single chain can't report R-hat, so whether it converges was not checked.\n- **Novelty** against the existing models was not checked either.\n\nFiles are in `…/experiment1/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_0/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":46428,"cache_read_input_tokens":11602,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":46428,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b9f49a8a-95b1-443c-b78e-fd89bad94b0f","uuid":"706fb2e9-a373-4b84-a77d-5f837f13929f","timestamp":"2026-10-04T17:54:42.766Z","request_id":"req_011CfhdF5uHS9S4CswcJQkyM"}
